---
{
  title: "get_object"
}
---
### NAME

    get_object() - Resolves a target object from a specifier string. Checks,
    in order: the 'me'/'here' keywords, the context object's inventory and
    its environment, livings by name, and finally a file path (loading it if
    necessary). The search context defaults to this_body() when no object is
    supplied.

### SYNOPSIS

    varargs object get_object( string str, object player );

### DESCRIPTION

    Resolves a target object from a specifier string. Checks, in order: the
    'me'/'here' keywords, the context object's inventory and its
    environment, livings by name, and finally a file path (loading it if
    necessary). The search context defaults to this_body() when no object is
    supplied.

### PARAMETERS

    str     (string)
            The object specifier.

    player  (object, optional)
            Context object for relative lookups; defaults to this_body()
            when not an object.

### RETURN VALUES

    (object) The first matching object, or 0 if none matched.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}get_object("sword");           // present in you or your environment
    get_object("me", this_body()); // yourself
    get_object("here");            // your environment{{di0}}
